1	//! Incremental zstd decoding over ruzstd (CLAUDE.md §5). The upload
2	//! verification pipeline streams a stored NAR through this decoder while a
3	//! hasher counts: a bomb is bounded by output accounting, never by buffer
4	//! size. Errors are typed and total: truncated frames, corrupt frames, and
5	//! over-limit output all answer in [`ZstdError`], and no input shape can
6	//! panic the decoder.
7	//!
8	//! The stream's contract with ruzstd: the frame decoder is invoked only
9	//! when the input pipe holds a watermark of [`ZSTD_BLOCK_WIRE_MAX`] bytes.
10	//! A zstd block body can never exceed 128 KiB on the wire, so every block
11	//! the decoder starts is guaranteed complete in its input, and a
12	//! mid-block truncation can only ever happen at a real end of input.
